            <ArticleTitle>Carvedilol for heart failure: more than just a beta-blocker?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>493-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Carvedilol is a non-selective beta-blocker, and the only one, in recent clinical trials, to have shown a clear reduction in mortality. It is suggested that, compared with other beta-blockers, carvedilol has additional advantageous effects in heart failure, and should be considered as part of the routine treatment of heart failure.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
